You are tasked with implementing a memoization decorator in Python to optimize the performance of a function. Memoization is a technique used to store the results of expensive function calls and return the cached result when the same inputs occur again. The provided code snippet shows a Python property decorated with a `memoized` decorator. Your task is to create a memoization decorator that can be used to cache the results of a function and improve its performance.

Your memoization decorator should be able to cache the results of a function and return the cached result when the same inputs are provided again. The decorator should work for functions with any number of arguments and should handle both positional and keyword arguments.

